          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-72786",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $U?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1 & -3+0 & 4+3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"
