          ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $-\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:=\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot 6 & \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot (-3) & \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot 9 & \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot 0\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"
